-- Source module: Solutions.KIL2Table
/-!
# KIL2: generating the offset table of a controlled shift

`genP Q ac` pushes onto stack `14` the table `tbl Q ac` of the offsets
`(Σ_k c_k · d_k) mod Q`, `p = (d_0, …, d_{r-1})` ranging over the mixed-radix shape
`ac.map Prod.fst` in increasing order (first field most significant), where `ac = [(a_k, c_k)]`.
It is built field by field from the last one: `T ← concat_{d < a} (T + c·d mod Q)`.
Everything (`a_k`, `c_k`, the suffix volumes) is a literal of the code.

* `genP_spec`: the generator, linear cost `O(|A| · (vol A + 1) · (Bb + 2))`.
* `tbl_eq_offs`: `tbl` is the table `(range (vol A)).map (offs Λ c A)` of `KILShift`.
